    "created_at": "2015-12-06T07:21:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-06T07:21:34Z",
    "body": "Maybe the length value changed over the air? Sounds like low hanging fruit\nwhich should have been checked for though.\nOn Dec 5, 2015 11:12 PM, \"WickedShell\" notifications@github.com wrote:\n\n> Basically it's trying to add a byte to the payload buffer when it runs out\n> of space. Unfortunately this seems to have been caused by an error over the\n> wire and I haven't been able to recreate it with a debugger. I'm not sure\n> how we managed to exceed the buffer length anywhere.\n> \n> Exception in thread \"COM8\" java.nio.BufferOverflowException\n> at java.nio.Buffer.nextPutIndex(Buffer.java:521)\n> at java.nio.HeapByteBuffer.put(HeapByteBuffer.java:169)\n> at com.MAVLink.Messages.MAVLinkPayload.add(MAVLinkPayload.java:25)\n> at com.MAVLink.Parser.mavlink_parse_char(Parser.java:79)\n> at swiftgcs.mavparser$parseBytes.invoke(mavparser.clj:124)\n> at serial.core$listen$reify__10359.serialEvent(core.clj:117)\n> at\n> purejavacomm.PureJavaSerialPort.sendDataEvents(PureJavaSerialPort.java:96)\n> at purejavacomm.PureJavaSerialPort.access$2500(PureJavaSerialPort.java:47)\n> at purejavacomm.PureJavaSerialPort$3.run(PureJavaSerialPort.java:1244)\n> at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:745)\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n> https://github.com/mavlink/mavlink/issues/474.\n",
