    "created_at": "2016-01-02T05:16:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-02T05:16:12Z",
    "body": "Alright managed to recreate this and attatch a debugger, and get a heap dump. It appears that the error is from https://github.com/mavlink/mavlink/blob/master/pymavlink/generator/java/lib/Parser.java#L97 basically if we didnt get they byte we expected for the CRC we check if its the start of a new packet. And then reset the state. This bypasses the normal resetting of the state that happens here https://github.com/mavlink/mavlink/blob/master/pymavlink/generator/java/lib/Parser.java#L46 which clears out the payload. This should be easy to correct, I'll get a PR in within the next couple of days.\n\nI also noticed that the payload size is set to 512 bytes, which is not a valid payload length (the max valid payload length is 255 so we are wasting a fair amount of space). I'll probably get a PR in for this at the same time.\n",
